{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:KnotsParticlesConfinement.HadronExists","@type":"LeanModule","name":"KnotsParticlesConfinement.HadronExists","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.ParticleInteractions.HadronDisplay"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hadron.exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hadron.exists","kind":"theorem","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/hadron-exists.lean#L21-L40","doc":"**Existence of hadrons.**\n\nA `Hadron` term exists. The intended witness is the proton\n`𝔭 = B₃(u, u, d)` (Borromean braid + Hopf gluon, satisfying\n`E_cross < 0`), but constructing that witness requires the full\nHecke-element + crossing-energy chain.\n\nFor pure existence, a `Hadron` with two `unknot` constituents\nsuffices — it is a degenerate witness (does not satisfy the\nphysical stability condition `E_cross < 0`), but it is a valid\ninhabitant of the `Hadron` type. Strengthening to \"a stable\nhadron exists\" is a follow-up requiring the binding-energy\nclassification on the constituents.\n","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:hadron-exists","label":"prop:hadron-exists","md":"quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/hadron-exists.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}